WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.250
Choose the route. A visitor requests a public poster. The content delivery network routes the request to a suitable edge location rather than always going directly to the origin.

2
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:23.000
Return a cached asset. If the edge has a valid copy, it returns that representation. This can reduce both response latency and repeated origin transfer.

3
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:32.083
Fetch on a miss. A missing or expired representation needs an origin fetch. The origin and its network path still matter for uncached work.

4
00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:42.917
Use a versioned URL. When asset bytes change, publish a new content-versioned name. Long-lived immutable caching only fits a URL whose content will not change.

5
00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:54.167
Separate private data. An account or booking response may be personal and time-sensitive. Do not place it on the shared public cache path without a deliberately safe policy.

6
00:00:54.167 --> 00:01:05.500
Measure each path. Compare edge hits, misses and private requests separately. A fast cached poster does not show whether the booking API meets its latency and correctness objectives.
